# Create Screen Rule

Use this rule when creating or updating any screen component.

## Required structure

- Screen UI implementation must be created under the owning feature's `screens/` subfolder: `components/features/<flow>/screens/...`.
- Use flow-based screen paths:
  - `components/features/auth/screens/<ScreenName>/index.tsx`
  - `components/features/main/screens/<ScreenName>/index.tsx`
- Additional flows (as needed by project growth) get their own feature folder with its own `index.ts` barrel:
  - `components/features/onboarding/screens/<ScreenName>/index.tsx`
  - `components/features/settings/screens/<ScreenName>/index.tsx`
- Route files under `app/...` should stay thin and only export/import screen components from that flow's `components/features/<flow>/index.ts` barrel (e.g. `export { ScreenNameScreen as default } from "@/components/features/<flow>";`) — never from the deep `screens/<ScreenName>` path directly.
- Every screen must be re-exported by name from its feature's `index.ts` barrel, with a `Screen` suffix on the exported alias to distinguish it from plain feature components (`export { default as ScreenNameScreen } from "./screens/ScreenName";`). The barrel is that feature's single entry point for anything outside the feature folder.
- Wrap every screen in `ScreenWrapper` (`components/shared/layout/ScreenWrapper`). It renders the auth layout (logo header, auth padding) by default; pass `variant="main"` for main-flow screens. Use its props (`isScrollable`, `justifyContent`, `paddingSize`, `showHeader`, `style`, ...) instead of re-creating a screen container.
- Follow component directory structure boundaries from `component-structure.mdc`.
- Prefer composing with existing shared/feature-scoped components before creating new primitives.

```tsx
// app/(auth)/login/index.tsx
export { LoginScreen as default } from "@/components/features/auth";

// components/features/auth/index.ts
export { default as LoginScreen } from "./screens/Login";

// components/features/main/screens/Home/index.tsx
import ScreenWrapper from "@/components/shared/layout/ScreenWrapper";
import { Text } from "@/components/shared/ui";

export default function Home() {
  return (
    <ScreenWrapper variant="main">
      <Text variant="H3">HOME</Text>
    </ScreenWrapper>
  );
}
```

## UI conventions

- Use `Text` from `@/components/shared/ui` (implemented in `components/shared/ui/Text/Base`) for all user-facing text.
- Use `Icon` from `@/components/shared/ui/Icon` for icons.
- Use `Spacing` tokens (`@/constants/Spacing`) first in styles; use `moderateScale` (`@/constants/Metrics`) only when a token does not exist.
- Keep styles in colocated `styles.ts`.

## Navigation and routing

- If a new screen is added under `app/`, ensure route wiring is complete (stack/tab where needed).
- Do not leave temporary test navigation in production flows unless explicitly requested.

## Translation

- No hardcoded user-facing strings.
- Add translation keys in both `locale/en.json` and `locale/ar.json` in the same change.

## Validation

- Run formatter/lint on changed files.
- Ensure no unrelated files are modified.
